<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>Downloads the current release of Audacity for Windows (the 64-bit x86_64 .msi asset of the newest non-pre-release on GitHub that has a matching file, kept under the asset's own file name) and checks it against the SHA-256 that GitHub records for the asset. When the asset has no recorded digest the run stops with an error and writes nothing: the program is then a hand import until a release with a digest exists. The asset names, sizes and digest flags were read from GitHub's release list on 2026-11-13 (the newest 30 releases): from 4.0.0 on the project names the installer like audacity-win-4.0.2-x86_64.msi (with an arm64 MSI beside it) and GitHub records a digest for it; the releases of the 3.x line have .exe installers and no MSI, so the pattern matches none of their files. AutoPkg takes the first release that has a matching file however old it is, so a new spelling of the name would send the recipe back to an older release; read the line that names the selected asset and release in the first dry run. The recipe never stops on an unchanged download, so a failed import is tried again at the next run. Pre-releases are skipped unless the override sets the input include_prereleases to true. The step GitHubNewestReleaseGuard, right after the provider, stops the run when the release that the provider selected is not the newest release (a pre-release is skipped unless include_prereleases is true): it names the newest release and its files. The project may publish a 3.x maintenance release after a 4.x one: that release has .exe files only and no MSI, so the guard stops the run until the override's release_tag_pattern names the 4.x line (for example Audacity-4\.); every run then names the newer releases that the pattern left out. The override's input accepted_newest_release, set to the tag of a newest release that has no Windows installer file (.msi, .exe, .msix) on purpose, lets the run go on only while that release is the newest. The MSI was not downloaded or installed: its version, install behaviour and publisher are not established.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.Audacity-Win</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>Audacity</string>
            <key>SEARCH_PATTERN</key>
            <string>audacity-win-[0-9.]+-x86_64\.msi$</string>
            <key>accepted_newest_release</key>
            <string></string>
            <key>include_prereleases</key>
            <false/>
            <key>release_tag_pattern</key>
            <string></string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>GitHubReleasesInfoProvider</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>github_repo</key>
                    <string>audacity/audacity</string>
                    <key>asset_regex</key>
                    <string>%SEARCH_PATTERN%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.SharedProcessors/GitHubNewestReleaseGuard</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>github_asset_api_url</key>
                    <string>%asset_url%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>URLDownloader</string>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>EndOfCheckPhase</string>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.SharedProcessors/GitHubAssetDigest</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>github_asset_api_url</key>
                    <string>%asset_url%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.SharedProcessors/ChecksumVerifier</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>pathname</key>
                    <string>%pathname%</string>
                    <key>expected_sha256</key>
                    <string>%expected_sha256%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
